  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given $f(x)=\\log (1+x)-\\frac{2 x}{2+x}$<br />$\\begin{aligned}<br />& f^{\\prime}(x)=\\frac{1}{1+x}-\\frac{(2+x)(2)-2 x}{(2+x)^2} \\\\<br />& =\\frac{1}{1+x}-\\frac{4}{(2+x)^2} \\\\<br />& =\\frac{(2+x)^2-4-4 x}{(1+x)(2+x)^2}=\\frac{x^2}{(1+x)(2+x)^2}>0 \\text { for all } \\\\<br />& x \\in(0, \\infty)<br />\\end{aligned}$<br />Thus, given function $\\mathrm{f}(\\mathrm{x})$ is increasing on $(0$, $\\infty)$.",
    "image": null
  },
